= Question 38

Describe how to determine the equation of the horizontal asymptote of a rational function when the

degree of the polynomial in the numerator and the degree of the polynomial in the denominator are

equal.

== Solution

The horizontal asymptote is $y = frac(a ,b )$ where $a $ is the leading coefficient in the numerator and $b $

is the leading coefficient in the denominator.

or

Use polynomial division to divide the numerator by the denominator. The equation of the

horizontal asymptote will have the same value as the quotient.

